<section class="section">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <h1>Refund policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 20 September 2026</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Before we start work</h2>
      <p>
        If you cancel before we begin design, we refund the full amount you paid, less any
        domain registration fee we have already spent on your behalf. Domain fees paid to a
        registrar cannot be recovered once the domain is registered.
      </p>

      <h2>After work has started</h2>
      <p>
        Once design has begun, we refund according to how much of the project is complete:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Design stage:</strong> we keep 40% of the project fee as work completed.</li>
        <li><strong>Build stage:</strong> we keep 70% of the project fee as work completed.</li>
        <li><strong>After launch:</strong> the project fee is not refundable, but you keep the delivered site.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If we cannot deliver what we agreed, we refund the unearned portion in full.
      </p>

      <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        Subscription billing is refundable on a pro-rata basis for the unused part of the current
        period if you cancel within the first seven days. After seven days, cancellation stops the
        next renewal and the current period runs to its end without a refund.
      </p>

      <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
      <p>
        Open a support ticket from your account dashboard and select <em>Billing</em>, or email
        <a href="mailto:<%= settings.supportEmail || 'support@woohelperpro.com' %>"><%= settings.supportEmail || 'support@woohelperpro.com' %></a>.
        Include your order or invoice number. We answer refund requests within three business days
        and pay approved refunds within ten business days.
      </p>

      <h2>Refund method</h2>
      <p>
        Refunds go back to the method you paid with where technically possible — bKash, Nagad and
        Rocket refunds are returned to the same wallet number. Bank transfers are returned to the
        originating account.
      </p>

      <h2>Exceptions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Third-party costs already paid (domain registration, paid licenses, ad spend).</li>
        <li>Custom integrations bought specifically for your project from a third party.</li>
        <li>Accounts suspended for breaching our terms of service.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
